<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leo Sgouros</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1208</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leo Sgouros was a Byzantine Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> and Corinth in the years around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>. Taking advantage of weakening imperial authority, he extended his power into central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. He was the chief opponent of the Frankish conquerors of southern Greece and held out in the citadel of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acrocorinth">Acrocorinth</a> until his death around 1208.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leo-sgouros.jpg" alt="Leo Sgouros" width="320" height="307" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ArisMethymna · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leo_Sgouros_seal.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
